/-!
# Conditional outside-H endpoints in the SL₃ closure branch

The actual O²(H) lies in Y, and C=⟨R₁,O²(H),X₁⟩ acts on W/V₁ with its
literal commutator kernel. B.6.8 supplies normalization of C_T(W) and
placement of the selected H's action kernel in its maximal-overgroup core.
The odd endpoint uses T∩K, with T=T_L and T∩L≤K still explicit. The even
endpoint lifts an abelian multiplicity action to preservation of V; a
faithful odd-order plane image supplies that abelianness.

The marked multiplicity embedding, Sylow kernel, residual p-group and
cyclic-image calculation, order-three moved subgroup, and odd-degree
`T=T_L` geometry are provided by the dedicated modules in this directory.
Their endpoint theorems retain the exact preceding source hypotheses and the
original selected H.
Source: Aschbacher--Smith, combined manuscript, printed p.782.
-/
